# utcToCst and cstToUtc return new values, leaving their input unchanged.
2024-01-02T12:00 d!
@d utcToCst isoDateTimeFmt wl
@d isoDateTimeFmt wl
@d cstToUtc isoDateTimeFmt wl
@d isoDateTimeFmt wl

# A literal evaluated repeatedly gives the same value each time.
(2024-01-02T12:00 utcToCst isoDateTimeFmt wl) q!
@q x
@q x
